[{:db/id "q-81737/selection/7fbaa7793f163f82454e5e7f9b6c95223b629cdf97fb364dba99ec4b6a58f306" :answer/id #uuid "084d6fb5-1145-5d40-8082-7323b55834ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=12{x}^{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}-\\frac{x}{y}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737/selection/76cc84dcd3402c6548e567139ff4baa066f11a1fa95d53308a341b3bb53d0024" :answer/id #uuid "943ef10b-a598-5663-a926-af18c265095b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{y}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737/selection/e3584a0c9104ad8cd8a9ae04f84dc2925aec154936e4dba7c132409cf6727f0b" :answer/id #uuid "1fa9c242-dfa9-5339-a37d-3f3ad4778e56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=12{x}^{3}y-\\frac{x}{y}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737/selection/40fd6325fef50822e00ddc400be5a9129567f76d380da21f1ae938b4438332d3" :answer/id #uuid "baf3329c-ec0b-5776-90be-611bc51dfed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737/selection/210508842f32d1048c6ea565c562d0dcfc2547a9026fc886e988d6a8c3ffb666" :answer/id #uuid "e3458a7e-ccf3-541d-bb91-4a16aa05357c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f687fd7b-0748-53fe-89b3-940ba8bde874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81737/selection/210508842f32d1048c6ea565c562d0dcfc2547a9026fc886e988d6a8c3ffb666" :answer-field/choices ["q-81737/selection/7fbaa7793f163f82454e5e7f9b6c95223b629cdf97fb364dba99ec4b6a58f306" "q-81737/selection/76cc84dcd3402c6548e567139ff4baa066f11a1fa95d53308a341b3bb53d0024" "q-81737/selection/e3584a0c9104ad8cd8a9ae04f84dc2925aec154936e4dba7c132409cf6727f0b" "q-81737/selection/40fd6325fef50822e00ddc400be5a9129567f76d380da21f1ae938b4438332d3" "q-81737/selection/210508842f32d1048c6ea565c562d0dcfc2547a9026fc886e988d6a8c3ffb666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81737" :question/id #uuid "a4cd2d9c-aa9c-533b-b610-fc91804dad9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81737" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ where $F(x,y)=(12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,i+(\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}})\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ g(y) & =\\frac{1}{y}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=\\frac{1}{y}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81737/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81737"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection/d488088c48aad9d2ba4a1bf470a4c8ac7adde89e50f84e19189fa313cec3e4b6" :answer/id #uuid "26bb2150-bd4d-5ee4-a519-ae7cf9d85f64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection/cc1f3f04deebc55de0ac05c50b8389274b4c514b27b1548523ba863996620607" :answer/id #uuid "1af6b8fa-ad47-5b32-81c5-408484fa026d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection/497301b7bdb545111372adf02bf8da16f6e277710f7ad66cf00e542cd580f5b8" :answer/id #uuid "54f8a568-c21f-5a39-b16a-2db3381ef317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection/9bbb5017d513212a07abe5c696f974ad35470bc246d0d8a3554221cfb73ef6ce" :answer/id #uuid "1ba7c4f6-95a4-54f4-839c-ab7995e838c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection/1838bf1e03a86186cc679a519ef3547978febc6500779e906edbcb7512b80387" :answer/id #uuid "d5ed65ed-d417-5fa7-b74a-9d69f889aad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=(x+y){e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e509f71-ed01-57c1-9d73-52287c9b0ee5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81741/selection/497301b7bdb545111372adf02bf8da16f6e277710f7ad66cf00e542cd580f5b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-81741/selection/d488088c48aad9d2ba4a1bf470a4c8ac7adde89e50f84e19189fa313cec3e4b6" "q-81741/selection/cc1f3f04deebc55de0ac05c50b8389274b4c514b27b1548523ba863996620607" "q-81741/selection/497301b7bdb545111372adf02bf8da16f6e277710f7ad66cf00e542cd580f5b8" "q-81741/selection/9bbb5017d513212a07abe5c696f974ad35470bc246d0d8a3554221cfb73ef6ce" "q-81741/selection/1838bf1e03a86186cc679a519ef3547978febc6500779e906edbcb7512b80387"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81741" :question/id #uuid "def26eac-f7dd-5378-8a75-b8b2f9ba1f34" :question/math-academy-id "q-81741" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}\\,i+x{e}^{xy}\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(z) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z) \\\\ h(z) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81741/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection/bb08c35a44ef95f3ab58bed7cf2bbe547ee38e0cb3f87029360e1c5ff54a670d" :answer/id #uuid "66bd6623-0740-536c-941c-e7c3aa1f86ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=x{e}^{xy}+2+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection/26e082ba3147761a3a82630410f62cf0b40db63bae436da38cd169b41d6b5d2b" :answer/id #uuid "56953072-83dd-53c5-bd82-21711aa98f61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection/90ccfe250d4d4da777baf28c53cc6168df635da3c664bb9612175792fc2f14d2" :answer/id #uuid "ba8db0b3-97b6-51d8-b18e-4053a330473d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection/ed201df88b94eb7700e72130b6ba2c25c19979e1a45f44da6a494123f5ae2994" :answer/id #uuid "68ecce04-ff69-553c-a616-7a58a97ee24b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+xy+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection/a1b83d141ec3130490efe880535419311e6cb0ebedf52c18a300b1902b2b5141" :answer/id #uuid "658ec369-19b5-52ad-b51f-1b14f85d8320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=xy{e}^{xy}+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5754676-fd25-51bd-89a3-fabf150ef837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81749/selection/90ccfe250d4d4da777baf28c53cc6168df635da3c664bb9612175792fc2f14d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-81749/selection/bb08c35a44ef95f3ab58bed7cf2bbe547ee38e0cb3f87029360e1c5ff54a670d" "q-81749/selection/26e082ba3147761a3a82630410f62cf0b40db63bae436da38cd169b41d6b5d2b" "q-81749/selection/90ccfe250d4d4da777baf28c53cc6168df635da3c664bb9612175792fc2f14d2" "q-81749/selection/ed201df88b94eb7700e72130b6ba2c25c19979e1a45f44da6a494123f5ae2994" "q-81749/selection/a1b83d141ec3130490efe880535419311e6cb0ebedf52c18a300b1902b2b5141"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81749" :question/id #uuid "569f8015-7dc4-5a18-8474-832c2e68650b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81749" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ where $F(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}\\text{ }i+(x{e}^{xy}+2y)\\text{ }j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+2y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+2y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{xy}+2y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =2y \\\\ g(y) & ={y}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)={y}^{2}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81749/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81749"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection/3bdba45905a7a471638e996a732a4608753817a38ca24f2e1acb8c7502734fbe" :answer/id #uuid "d17bfb9a-8e07-559b-8fac-6af97f273834" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xz-{e}^{z}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection/fab5f1ba808fb8505bc1472708f3156917b80875d5d4849d64665803982a0d61" :answer/id #uuid "ae231568-11a6-5d3b-b716-61adf9c41929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz-y{e}^{z}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection/6a78465eaf8fde5b13d84d03475827490de414172f2417a34641e08653a70eb6" :answer/id #uuid "43657de1-8aab-5d63-bb61-a029e159baa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+yz-{e}^{z}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection/706ad30707e8d2c8ff3403c41fdc14be9418ccfb06a80302f91838c75134997e" :answer/id #uuid "4111b42c-485d-50ef-8134-b04c0b205a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-x{e}^{z}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection/a74d480f2caf38925c78e7017f7744f8f9a350dcf8e31d353d81e465efa11034" :answer/id #uuid "4083e5c0-fa10-5091-901b-60ddde4d0475" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27d0cb5f-d94b-5736-b8d7-1396257b6194" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124733/selection/a74d480f2caf38925c78e7017f7744f8f9a350dcf8e31d353d81e465efa11034" :answer-field/choices ["q-124733/selection/3bdba45905a7a471638e996a732a4608753817a38ca24f2e1acb8c7502734fbe" "q-124733/selection/fab5f1ba808fb8505bc1472708f3156917b80875d5d4849d64665803982a0d61" "q-124733/selection/6a78465eaf8fde5b13d84d03475827490de414172f2417a34641e08653a70eb6" "q-124733/selection/706ad30707e8d2c8ff3403c41fdc14be9418ccfb06a80302f91838c75134997e" "q-124733/selection/a74d480f2caf38925c78e7017f7744f8f9a350dcf8e31d353d81e465efa11034"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124733" :question/id #uuid "f6dd231c-6e98-5338-9bc2-ef1a31fa9648" :question/math-academy-id "q-124733" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,i+2xy{z}^{3}\\,j+(3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z})\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2xy{z}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) & =3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z} \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124733/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124733"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection/a390e9b85ca24fd945401501be8f087d0adb171ed7debcf48e8352cdf3effea3" :answer/id #uuid "59d31e27-0aa0-566f-ae20-67eb96b31839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y}+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection/526ded62cd4a8c5c67fad37f792dc30fad9114b7718d692db4322a26370c29d9" :answer/id #uuid "020e4eb5-f69a-52ce-a50d-34c8fbbce48b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=2y{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection/28df69303d1c2b157ce4d918630d7ec7af8857719755573b7268c6aeea98fbb1" :answer/id #uuid "3406d2d3-08a2-58d6-a4ba-b0fcd245209f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection/9da1972d1cd6811bd0944bcb909884575834eaf663152195edf072c2530bf302" :answer/id #uuid "7c516d5a-291b-57d6-9746-a24d02de40e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection/2f027b46b2d49988f8356767466f5cd770aa37148f401dd7f5c07fb7ad5aa0cf" :answer/id #uuid "ec60e2c0-ce80-5367-8b2b-a16c15b4acde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)=y{e}^{y}+x{y}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2133f6a4-f86a-564d-86bb-b566df8c38be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132080/selection/9da1972d1cd6811bd0944bcb909884575834eaf663152195edf072c2530bf302" :answer-field/choices ["q-132080/selection/a390e9b85ca24fd945401501be8f087d0adb171ed7debcf48e8352cdf3effea3" "q-132080/selection/526ded62cd4a8c5c67fad37f792dc30fad9114b7718d692db4322a26370c29d9" "q-132080/selection/28df69303d1c2b157ce4d918630d7ec7af8857719755573b7268c6aeea98fbb1" "q-132080/selection/9da1972d1cd6811bd0944bcb909884575834eaf663152195edf072c2530bf302" "q-132080/selection/2f027b46b2d49988f8356767466f5cd770aa37148f401dd7f5c07fb7ad5aa0cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132080" :question/id #uuid "56db4f7d-60e2-5a2d-b5c8-a70229b1b98b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132080" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+(x{e}^{y}+2y)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{y}+2y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =2y \\\\ g(y) & ={y}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)={y}^{2}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-132080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97730a2e-3d3e-5a2c-b366-7a3b1eafbe63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
